{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/772559-claimed-ghouls","id":772559,"title":"Claimed Ghouls","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-11-23T15:27:46-08:00","id":772559,"title":"Claimed Ghouls","content":"<b>Premise:</b> I want to make ghouls who are claimed by spirits. <br /> <br /> <b>Why?:</b><br /> <br /> My players are at war with a Circle of the Crone vampire cult. They are basically worshiping a rank 5 faith spirit (Longing Faith) in the shadow who is playing the part of their mother goddess. I read &quot;The Book of Spirits&quot; and I was fascinated by the idea of a vampire with Blood Tenebrous to fuse with a spirit, uniting beast, spirit, and vampire into a new and terrifying being. The discipline is called &quot;Drawing in the Devil&quot;. <br /> <br /> I want their high priestess to reach an apotheosis by binding herself with the spirit of faith. I can't just do that off the bat. I want to seed the possibility of this by having faithful ghouls become claimed by permission of their masters.<br /> <br /> <b>But...: </b>I do not care if it says or implies somewhere that ghouls cannot become claimed. I have done a little reading on it and I don't see why it would be an issue. In my setting almost all vampires consider themselves a blood sorcerers. The different covenants find exploring different forms of magic to be a good way to deal with the requiem. <br /> <br /> <b>Question: </b>What do you guys think would be a cool way to handle such things? Do they have a special name? <br /> <br /> <b>Current Ideas: </b>The ghouls will be claimed by Longing Faith's umia. So in particular I am looking at putting Ghouls together that are going to be claimed by faith spirits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8619-aforgeforthoughts","name":"AForgeForThoughts","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-23T15:48:09-08:00","id":772573,"title":"","content":"So what you're basically looking for is advice on something rather like the creations of a smaller-scale godlike being. Worth keeping that in mind, as even within the scope of playable mechanics there's a lot of stuff that's worked out by feel and narrative requirements.<br /> <br /> Worth pointing out and asking about<b></b>:<br /> <br /> Ancient elementals notwithstanding, one does not reach the Rank of <i>Dihir</i> without diversifying \u2014 Longing Faith is almost certainly going to be a spirit of more than just faith, which in turn is going to impact the resonance her brood in particular cultivates. What other associations does she have?<br /> <br /> Similarly, spirits have origins and histories that tend to influence their development and behavior \u2014 what events gave birth to Longing Faith, and how has she survived this long without being consumed?<br /> <br /> What's the cult like, particularly the high priestess? As with spirits, history is going to have a significant impact on a vampire's Vitae and things maintained with it. Is there a lot of blood-bonding within the vampiric section of the cult? Is there much in the way of a line of descent among the vampires or are they relatively unrelated individuals? What mix of clans is there? Who manages the ghouls' upkeep?<br /> <br /> What are the players' characters like? What would work best to contrast or complement the pack thematically?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-23T17:43:30-08:00","id":772669,"title":"","content":"Honestly I would model it a bit in a way Idigam servants are represented in core W:tF 2ed. I wouldn't go the way where lots of minor justice spirits claim ghouls, but I'd go with the powerful spirit through blood communion with vampire splitting a part of itself into blood, thus creating Hive-Claimed or weird spirit/flesh horrors a la those associated with passing of idigam. Each ghoul would take few different facets of spirit. I just put into search engine &quot;faith/longing synonyms&quot; and here I have spirit of certainty, yearning and dogma warping the flesh of ghouls. Those creatures suffer Essence bleed, but like ghouls have to take Essence/Vitae from their vampire master, so they don't kill people outright, but frantically hunt their victims, snatch them and prepare them to be consumed by vampire-spirit fusion &quot;mini-Idigam&quot;-thing that share its Essence with them. Of course at the beginning there might be just a little portion of spirit in vampire's blood, so it would just give some additional powers to ghouls, maybe a Dread Power or Totem-like buff.<br /> <br /> For vampire after merging with spirit I'd use Idigam powers like Divine Clay, Crazed Evolution and Mad Fecundity, also maybe give it 2 forms. <br /> <br /> Bonus points: Just before being defeated, it splits itself completely into many shards and tries to escape. Did new shartha just appeared? Can it threaten the world if being let free?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7871-miriander","name":"Miriander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"26"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-23T17:59:52-08:00","id":772679,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the response. Those are important questions. I will answer most of them so that if anyone else finds them useful in helping me. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/772559-claimed-ghouls?p=772573#post772573\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So what you're basically looking for is advice on something rather like the creations of a smaller-scale godlike being. Worth keeping that in mind, as even within the scope of playable mechanics there's a lot of stuff that's worked out by feel and narrative requirements.<br /> <br /> Worth pointing out and asking about<b></b>:<br /> <br /> Ancient elementals notwithstanding, one does not reach the Rank of <i>Dihir</i> without diversifying \u2014 Longing Faith is almost certainly going to be a spirit of more than just faith, which in turn is going to impact the resonance her brood in particular cultivates. What other associations does she have?<br /> <br /> Similarly, spirits have origins and histories that tend to influence their development and behavior \u2014 what events gave birth to Longing Faith, and how has she survived this long without being consumed?</div> </div> </div> </div>Longing Faith is a product of the midwest and started feeding off of the faith resonance of the ancient Wichita peoples. Other religions began to influence her after those people changed and were displaced. Eventually Christianity became the dominant form of expression. I am not sure how this should affect her resonance though. <br /> <br /> <b><i>Do the themes of the different religions somehow change her essence? Or should a powerful spirit like that be absorbing other ideological and emotional portfolios? </i></b><br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/772559-claimed-ghouls?p=772573#post772573\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What's the cult like, particularly the high priestess? As with spirits, history is going to have a significant impact on a vampire's Vitae and things maintained with it. Is there a lot of blood-bonding within the vampiric section of the cult? Is there much in the way of a line of descent among the vampires or are they relatively unrelated individuals? What mix of clans is there? Who manages the ghouls' upkeep?</div> </div> </div> </div>The core of them were from 15th century Italy who worship Grecco-Roman deities. They now reside in middle america. They each have their own mystery cults of mortals that take on a variety of forms. Above that are cults of ghouls surrounding the kindred themselves. Within this the vampires are part of a cult which see the High Priestess as truly blessed because she uniquely has a relationship with the shadow. Most all of them are decent competent Cruac sorcerers. <br /> <br /> They think Longing Faith is Hecate, or at least an avatar of hers. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/772559-claimed-ghouls?p=772573#post772573\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What are the players' characters like? What would work best to contrast or complement the pack thematically? </div> </div> </div> </div>The players wear the mask of being Navajo, but are Iron Masters. The politics of American Indians are really big were I am from so that is were that decision came from, so there is a lot of small town drama based off of a fictional Navajo community. However we want to avoid painful stereotypes of Native Americans.<br /> <br /> As a pack they care about politics and economics. They are attempting to control entertainment, law enforcement, and business in their town. They sort of view the Navajo communities economy as their &quot;Territory&quot; which should be honored in all things. Which is a really weird concept but cool for Iron Masters. <br /> <br /> I honestly didn't expect my players to go in this direction but they have gradually done so. <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7871-miriander\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7871\" data-vbnamecard=\"7871\">Miriander</a> <br /> <br /> Those are excellent suggestions thank you. All of those ideas were scary. And that is what I like about them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8619-aforgeforthoughts","name":"AForgeForThoughts","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-23T18:11:45-08:00","id":772686,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AForgeForThoughts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/772559-claimed-ghouls?p=772679#post772679\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Longing Faith is a product of the midwest and started feeding off of the faith resonance of the ancient Wichita peoples. Other religions began to influence her after those people changed and were displaced. Eventually Christianity became the dominant form of expression. I am not sure how this should affect her resonance though.<br /> <br /> <b><i>Do the themes of the different religions somehow change her essence? Or should a powerful spirit like that be absorbing other ideological and emotional portfolios? </i></b></div> </div> </div> </div>It's a little closer to the latter than the former \u2014 a spirit of high Rank tends to develop a favored symbolset as they outgrow the simpler definition of &quot;spirit of X,&quot; and that's going to leave its mark on the spirit's imagery and activity, which is then likely to bleed into the resonance of a group it's sponsoring.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The core of them were from 15th century Italy who worship Grecco-Roman deities. They now reside in middle america. They each have their own mystery cults of mortals that take on a variety of forms. Above that are cults of ghouls surrounding the kindred themselves. Within this the vampires are part of a cult which see the High Priestess as truly blessed because she uniquely has a relationship with the shadow. Most all of them are decent competent Cruac sorcerers.<br /> <br /> They think Longing Faith is Hecate, or at least an avatar of hers. </div> </div> </div>Besides the blood sorcery and Blood Tenebrous, what are the primary Disciplines used by the cult? In what capacity does Longing Faith act that makes them attribute the name of Hecate to her rather than, say, Persephone?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The players wear the mask of being Navajo, but are Iron Masters. The politics of American Indians are really big were I am from so that is were that decision came from, so there is a lot of small town drama based off of a fictional Navajo community. However we want to avoid painful stereotypes of Native Americans.<br /> <br /> As a pack they care about politics and economics. They are attempting to control entertainment, law enforcement, and business in their town. They sort of view the Navajo communities economy as their &quot;Territory&quot; which should be honored in all things. Which is a really weird concept but cool for Iron Masters.<br /> <br /> I honestly didn't expect my players to go in this direction but they have gradually done so. </div> </div> </div>And how have the pack come into conflict with Longing Faith's cult?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-23T19:44:29-08:00","id":772740,"title":"","content":"Actually, in the first edition crone book it mentions they aren't above blood bonding claimed servants, and in second edition claimed is a condition, not a template, so it's compatible with everything that doesn't have immunity to being possessed. <br /> <br /> Do you have the blood sorcery book? It has a bit about threnodies, merits vampires can have to enhance their disciplines by tapping into their beasts. The reason I mention it is because with a botch, the beast can detach itself and go walk about as an ephemeral being. <br /> <br /> The cult might want capture those things in an attempt to make beast claimed, or see what happens if you shove a spirit into the gaping hole after the beast leaves, or possibly feeding a beast to a spirit to see what happens. <br /> <br /> Since you mentioned that you wanted a slow revelation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-23T20:17:55-08:00","id":772758,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:13px\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/772559-claimed-ghouls?p=772686#post772686\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> It's a little closer to the latter than the former \u2014 a spirit of high Rank tends to develop a favored symbol set as they outgrow the simpler definition of &quot;spirit of X,&quot; and that's going to leave its mark on the spirit's imagery and activity, which is then likely to bleed into the resonance of a group it's sponsoring.<br /> <br /> In what capacity does Longing Faith act that makes them attribute the name of Hecate to her rather than, say, Persephone?</div> </div> </div> </div></span><br /> <br /> My idea was that Longing Faith has been urging the vampires during their ritual offerings of blood to her. Longing Faith doesn't know what Hecate is, she just knows they believe in it just like Christians do in Jesus. They believe she is Hecate so she adapts herself to that form. Maybe after awhile of gathering faiths from other religions, being able to remodel herself has become an important ability.<br /> <br /> You are right though I need to think about how she proves that she is Hecate to the Kindred. I guess she needs to make her present known to the high priestess and giver her guidance through the use of Numina and Influences. Hecate though is supposed to be a Goddess of Magic, and Longing Faith has introduced a variety of magical resources to the cult. Examples are stolen Uratha artifacts, a human shaman, and even a Purified who serves Longing Faith .<br /> <br /> A lot of this isn't definite, so I am open to suggestions about how to use this idea differently.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/772559-claimed-ghouls?p=772686#post772686\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I<br /> Besides the blood sorcery and Blood Tenebrous, what are the primary Disciplines used by the cult?<br /> And how have the pack come into conflict with Longing Faith's cult?</div> </div> </div> </div>The chronicle started with a sheriff in their community dying. Basically the vampires had a human shaman offer essence to a spirit to go and kill the Sheriff. The pack picked up on this and it eventually led to them running into their Harpy. A packmember had the &quot;Other&quot; trigger and witnessed the vampire using domination on a self-help group she commanded. He went into death rage and killed the vampire and a few mystery cultists.<br /> <br /> Now the Kindred &quot;Sheriff&quot; has been in a steady conflict with the pack. She is one of the more mundane of cultists, focusing on transmutation blood sorcery and control of humans through narcotics.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/772559-claimed-ghouls?p=772740#post772740\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <span style=\"font-size:13px\">The cult might want capture those things in an attempt to make beast claimed, or see what happens if you shove a spirit into the gaping hole after the beast leaves, or possibly feeding a beast to a spirit to see what happens.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:13px\">Since you mentioned that you wanted a slow revelation.</span></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><br /> <br /> That is a clever story seed!</span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8619-aforgeforthoughts","name":"AForgeForThoughts","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-24T08:00:12-08:00","id":773117,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't rule out the possibility of a claimed ghoul developing some strange dread powers based on their condition. Like the ability to drink blood for essence, or an immunity to blood bonds...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-24T18:27:38-08:00","id":773560,"title":"","content":"Oh, in Ancient Bloodlines, there's also the Edimmu, the results of an ancient babylonian ritual, seven random spirits in a vampire meat suit, although they basically use spirit rules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}